 "result_text": "`idna.decode(b'\\x8d\\xd2')` now raises `IDNAError` instead of `UnicodeDecodeError`. I ran that input and a second one, `b'xn--a\\x8d'`, and both raise `IDNAError('Invalid ASCII in A-label')`. I didn't run the test suite or add tests. The changes are in `idna/core.py`:\n\n- **ASCII decoding in `encode` and `decode`:** non-ASCII bytes are caught and re-raised as `IDNAError`. `encode` had the same flaw, so I fixed both.\n- **Punycode decoding in `ulabel`:** a bad Punycode label now raises `IDNAError` instead of a raw `UnicodeError`. I didn't trigger this path with an input.\n- **Trailing-hyphen check in `ulabel`:** it now looks at the last byte directly instead of decoding it to ASCII first, so it can't raise a decode error.\n\nThe message \"Invalid ASCII in A-label\" is slightly off for the top-level `encode`/`decode` case, where the bad bytes are in the whole domain rather than one label. I kept one message for both; say if you want it reworded.",
